    "issue": "eda07788",
    "purpose": "consumer-family",
    "description": "Exploratory pilot for the DVB-T2 ETSI EN 302 755 v1.4.1 SS6.1.3 bit interleaver (parity interleaving composed with column twisting). Every cell is a whole-consumer comparison of two arms of the same operation on the same seeded frame. The baseline arm is always the established gf2 implementation and the candidate arm is always the arm whose lead needs attribution, so a speedup above 1 means the candidate is ahead: above 1 in a `-gap-` cell means the xdsopl/LDPC comparator is ahead of gf2, above 1 in a `-control-` cell means the `-C target-cpu=native` gf2 build is ahead of the conservative-portable gf2 control. This pilot sizes the family's measurement resolution from the `-null-` identity cell and covers the Short FECFRAME and streaming working sets the confirmatory family does not measure. No cell here decides adoption."
  },
  "frozen": {
